Have you already looked at the docs in this file:<br><a href="http://uk.geocities.com/olivier_rebellion/Polycolly.zip" class="postlink">http://uk.geocities.com/olivier_rebellion/Polycolly.zip</a> <br>It has tutorial for the time of impact and contact generation in the 2D case. <br><br>You will get more response on such questions in the gamedev.net forum:<br><a href="http://www.gamedev.net/community/forums/forum.asp?forum_id=20" class="postlink">http://www.gamedev.net/community/forums ... orum_id=20</a><br><br>For example, see this thread:<br><a href="http://www.gamedev.net/community/forums/topic.asp?topic_id=335494&amp;whichpage=1&amp;#2181700" class="postlink">http://www.gamedev.net/community/forums ... 1&amp;#2181700</a><br><br>But even in the gamedev.net forum, its best to give more details about your problem, like what kind of shapes do you want to support etc.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Tue Dec 27, 2005 9:18 pm</p><hr />
