		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Paper: Collision detection for moving polyhedra]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/viewtopic.php?p=532#p532"><![CDATA[
You can download this paper from MIT here:<br><br><a href="http://www.ai.mit.edu/research/publications/browse/0800browse.shtml" class="postlink">http://www.ai.mit.edu/research/publicat ... owse.shtml</a><br><br>The approach in this paper is a Parameterized Sweep.<br><br>If you are interested in calculating the time of impact, you can read some papers by Stephane Redon here:<br><a href="http://i3d.inrialpes.fr/~redon/" class="postlink">http://i3d.inrialpes.fr/~redon/</a><br><br>"An Algebraic Solution to the Problem of Collision Detection for Rigid Polyhedral Objects", "CONTACT" and "Fast Continuous Collision Detection between Rigid Bodies".<br><br>You might also want to read my draft paper here: <a href="http://www.continuousphysics.com/BulletContinuousCollisionDetection.pdf" class="postlink">http://www.continuousphysics.com/Bullet ... ection.pdf</a> <br><br>Erwin<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=2">Erwin Coumans</a> — Tue Dec 27, 2005 6:16 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
